* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored dependencies: stored byte for byte, never converted. Any line-ending
# conversion would invalidate bin/lib/MANIFEST.sha256 at clone time.
bin/lib/** -text

# Scope of the deployable archive (spec section 12.1): tests/, tools/ and DEVNOTES.md
# live in the repository, never in the installed app. `git archive` therefore leaves them
# out, along with the repository's own service files.
#
# DEVNOTES.md carries the development notes: architecture, measurements, design decisions
# and the exhaustive operator reference. It is written for whoever changes this code, not
# for whoever runs it, and the operator README is self-sufficient without it.
tests/         export-ignore
DEVNOTES.md    export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
.gitignore     export-ignore

# tools/ is excluded file by file rather than as a directory, because the two
# re-validation procedures ship (spec section 14.1, deliverable 4). The contract declares
# them a prerequisite to any real use - `revalidate_app_acl_mapping.py` for the family
# table of `editappacl`, `revalidate_mapping.py` for the endpoint table of `editacl` - and
# the installation section names both. A prerequisite the operator cannot reach from the
# installed app is a prerequisite in name only, and the README's pointer at it would fall
# under the no-dangling-reference clause of deliverable 9: the clause would be contradicted
# by its own document. Of the two ways out, dropping the pointer or shipping the artefact,
# only the second keeps the requirement.
#
# The criterion is the contract's own - what it declares a prerequisite, and nothing else -
# and the exception does not generalize beyond it. Every other file here is development
# tooling and stays out. Both procedures read and neither writes; both import only
# `bin/acltools`, which ships, so they run from the installed app.
#
# A directory-wide `export-ignore` is not used, since git prunes the whole tree and no
# per-file exception can be carved back out of it. A test therefore sweeps `tools/` file by
# file, so that a new file added there cannot ship by omission.
tools/__pycache__/           export-ignore
tools/acl_probe_bootstrap.sh export-ignore
tools/acl_probe_bootstrap_rest.py export-ignore
tools/hash_manifest.py       export-ignore
tools/requirements-vendor.txt export-ignore
tools/vendor.sh              export-ignore
tools/verify_vendor.sh       export-ignore
